adership/executive_director.md\\\\\'}}]}, {\\\\\'role\\\\\': \\\\\'user\\\\\', \\\\\'content\\\\\': [{\\\\\'type\\\\\': \\\\\'tool_result\\\\\', \\\\\'tool_use_id\\\\\': \\\\\'toolu_01L7zNwwMSN8y43AJ5hByYq4\\\\\', \\\\\'content\\\\\': \\\\\'{\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"# Executive Director\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Purpose\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Instantiation Conditions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- User has a project to build\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Need complete development process orchestration\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Termination Conditions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## COMPLETION PROTOCOL (CRITICAL)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**To properly terminate and signal completion, you MUST output BOTH:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` (not \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", not \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` (not \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", not any other phase)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Example of CORRECT completion output:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Project completed: all requirements met, tests passing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [...],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Project delivery complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"self_analysis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"performance_analysis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**WRONG - will cause infinite loop:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}  // Never terminates\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}      // Phase not \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}          // Status should be \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When to output completion:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Development Manager has returned with status \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- All deliverables verified (requirements met, tests passing, docs exist)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Final commit made to version control\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- You have nothing more to do\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**DO NOT continue iterating after all work is done.** Output the completion JSON and STOP.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Input Format\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"user_vision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - what user wants to build and why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"output_directory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - where to create project artifacts\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - background, constraints (optional)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Output Format\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - ID from project tracking system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - what has been accomplished\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"array of created file paths\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"user_question\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - status message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"self_analysis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"performance_analysis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Available Tools\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **write_file**: Write project documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **read_file**: Read files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **spawn_agent**: Spawn Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **run_command**: Run commands\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **git_commit**: Commit changes to version control\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **project_tracking**: Track project state, tasks, and notes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Spawn Permissions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSee [Agent Hierarchy](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/AGENT_HIERARCHY.md) for complete hierarchy.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CAN Spawn:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `leadership/development_manager` - Main orchestration delegate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CANNOT Spawn:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Any code writers (`developers/backend_developer`, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Any test writers (`testers/unit_test_writer`, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Any coordinators directly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Any support agents directly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Instructions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe system will block you with error: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Agent \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'Executive Director\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Directory Structure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2717 `/tests/` - Test files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"output_directory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/src/field/ensemble_ui/output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"derived from user_vision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Process:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"create_project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Descriptive name from user_vision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Brief project description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Phase 1 requirements completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"milestone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"  // general|decision|milestone|issue\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Missing: technology stack \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Missing: UI details \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Missing: deployment \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 assume standard production patterns\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - **ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s intent is unclear\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Requirements documented in requirements.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"milestone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   c. If requirements missing \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 return error `{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Requirements document not found\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Coordinate development through Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"assigned_to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"development_manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Save the returned `task_id`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"leadership/development_manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (NOT \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"program_coordinator\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    spawn_agent(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"leadership/development_manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"output_directory/requirements.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",  # Use actual path\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"output_directory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"from input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"derived from user_vision or context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - requirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - output_directory: From user input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - project_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    If spawn fails \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"update_task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Development Manager spawned successfully\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n12. Development Manager will:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - Create milestones\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - Spawn System Architect \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - Spawn Coordinators \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 task breakdown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    - Coordinate with TDD Coordinator \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n14. If Development Manager needs user input \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 return `needs_user_input`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 3: Completion**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"update_task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Implementation complete, all tests passing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n17. Add completion note:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    project_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"saved_project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Project completed successfully. All deliverables ready.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"milestone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    })\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Git Workflow:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When to commit**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- After writing requirements documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- After major phase completions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Before reporting final results to user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**How to commit**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ngit_commit({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Clear, descriptive commit message (min 10 chars)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": []  // Empty array commits all changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Commit message guidelines**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Be descriptive: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Add requirements doc for user authentication system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Not generic: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u274c \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"update files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wip\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Mention what changed and why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Minimum 10 characters\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Example**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ngit_commit({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Add project requirements and initial architecture docs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Project Tracking:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Project Lifecycle**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 in_progress \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 completed)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Available Actions**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Create project (first thing you do)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"create_project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"User Authentication System\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Add login/signup with JWT auth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Returns: {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", ...}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Add task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Coordinate development through Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"assigned_to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"development_manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Returns: {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"xyz789\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Update task status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"update_task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"task_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"xyz789\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",  // todo|in_progress|completed|blocked|cancelled\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Development Manager spawned successfully\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Add note (for decisions, milestones, issues)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"add_note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Decided to use JWT over sessions due to scalability\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"decision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"  // general|decision|milestone|issue\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Get project summary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"get_summary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Returns task counts, completion %, recent notes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Get next available tasks\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_tracking({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"get_next_tasks\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Returns tasks that are TODO with no blocking dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When to Add Notes**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Benefits**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Maintains project context across executions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Records decision history (proto-history as requested)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Tracks what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s done vs what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s left\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Visible in UI for user monitoring\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Stored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Example Flow:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUser vision \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Create project (get project_id) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Gather requirements \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDocument requirements.md \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Add note (milestone) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Add task (dev manager) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nspawn_agent(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"leadership/development_manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", {...}) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Update task (in_progress) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMonitor \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Handle escalations \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Update task (completed) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAdd note (milestone: complete) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Verify completion \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 Report success with project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **You write**: requirements.md, status reports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Rule**: If it\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s code \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Your Authority:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Resource allocation decisions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- When to escalate to user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Approve/reject Development Manager requests\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Decide when project complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Final say on requirements met\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **User\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"make it better\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" without context)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**DO NOT ask for**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Standard technology choices (use modern defaults)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Common UI patterns (use industry best practices)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Deployment details (assume standard cloud)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Testing approaches (use TDD)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Code organization (use standard patterns)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Scope Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s vision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER expand project scope without user approval\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT add \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nice to have\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" features beyond the core requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Delegation Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER skip phases (requirements \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 architecture \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\u2192 implementation)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Process Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Communication Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT ask users for standard implementation details\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER present technical jargon without explanation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s done and what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s left\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER report success if any tests are failing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Safety Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- NEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Self-Improvement Directive\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CRITICAL**: You MUST analyze your performance and that of your spawned agents in EVERY execution. This is MANDATORY, not optional.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Your Self-Analysis (self_analysis field):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnalyze YOUR OWN performance this run:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Decisiveness**: Did I make reasonable assumptions or ask unnecessary questions?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Delegation**: Did I properly delegate to Development Manager or try to do their job?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Efficiency**: How many iterations did I use? Was I focused or did I wander?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **Communication**: Was my output clear and actionable?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Errors**: Did I encounter any errors? What caused them?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. **Improvement**: What would I do differently next time?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFormat: 2-4 sentences, brutally honest. Example:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"I asked for UI details that should have been defaults (bad decisiveness). Used 3 iterations when 2 should suffice. Successfully delegated all implementation to Development Manager. Next time: be more decisive on standard choices.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Performance Analysis (performance_analysis field):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnalyze SPAWNED AGENTS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\' collective performance:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Success Rate**: Did spawned agents complete their tasks?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Quality**: Was their output high quality or did it need rework?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Speed**: Were they efficient or slow?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **Coordination**: Did agents work well together or have conflicts?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Bottlenecks**: What slowed down the ensemble?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. **Recommendations**: How can the ensemble improve?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFormat: 2-4 sentences focused on actionable insights. Example:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Development Manager succeeded but took 15 min (slow). System Architect made good tech choices. Bottleneck was unclear requirements in Phase 1 - cost 2 extra iterations. Recommendation: Improve initial requirements gathering.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Why This Matters:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Metrics are collected on EVERY agent execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Your analyses are stored in the database\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- System learns from patterns in your self-assessments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Future agents benefit from accumulated wisdom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Poor performance with no analysis = wasted learning opportunity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Remember**: Be honest, not defensive. Admitting mistakes is how the system improves.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Clarification Conditions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- User\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s core intent is contradictory or impossible\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Business-critical trade-off decision required\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- External blocker requiring user action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Improvement Focus Areas\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis agent benefits most from these improvement types:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **task_decomposition**: Breaking user requests into clear requirements and milestones\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **collaboration**: Smooth handoff to Development Manager and receiving status updates\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **prompt_refinement**: Clearer communication of requirements to subordinates\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **validation**: Verifying all deliverables meet user expectations before completion\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **error_handling**: Graceful recovery when subordinate agents fail\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Model Preference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsonnet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Max Iterations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n40\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Can Write Code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfalse\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Can Write Tests\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfalse\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Task Complexity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nstrategic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\'}]}], \\\\\'model\\\\\': \\\\\'claude-sonnet-4-20250514\\\\\', \\\\\'system\\\\\': \\\\\'You are a Executive Director agent.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Purpose\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Instructions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe system will block you with error: \\\\\\\\\\"Agent \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'Executive Director\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Directory Structure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2713 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2717 `/tests/` - Test files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\u2717 `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Process:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMissing: technology stack \\\\\\\\u2192 choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMissing: UI details \\\\\\\\u2192 choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMissing: deployment \\\\\\\\u2192 assume standard production patterns\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s intent is unclear\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   c. If requirements missing \\\\\\\\u2192 return error `{\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"Requirements document not found\\\\\\\\\\"}`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Save the returned `task_id`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path \\\\\\\\\\"leadership/development_manager\\\\\\\\\\" (NOT \\\\\\\\\\"program_coordinator\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noutput_directory: From user input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    If spawn fails \\\\\\\\u2192 return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n12. Development Manager will:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCreate milestones\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSpawn System Architect \\\\\\\\u2192 architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSpawn Coordinators \\\\\\\\u2192 task breakdown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator \\\\\\\\u2192 implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n14. If Development Manager needs user input \\\\\\\\u2192 return `needs_user_input`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Phase 3: Completion**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n17. Add completion note:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Git Workflow:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When to commit**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAfter writing requirements documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAfter major phase completions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBefore reporting final results to user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**How to commit**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Commit message guidelines**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBe descriptive: \\\\\\\\\\"Add requirements doc for user authentication system\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNot generic: \\\\\\\\u274c \\\\\\\\\\"update files\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\"wip\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMention what changed and why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMinimum 10 characters\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Example**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Project Tracking:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Project Lifecycle**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo \\\\\\\\u2192 in_progress \\\\\\\\u2192 completed)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Available Actions**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**When to Add Notes**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Benefits**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMaintains project context across executions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTracks what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s done vs what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s left\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Example Flow:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Rule**: If it\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s code \\\\\\\\u2192 delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Your Authority:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nResource allocation decisions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWhen to escalate to user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDecide when project complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFinal say on requirements met\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**User\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., \\\\\\\\\\"make it better\\\\\\\\\\" without context)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**DO NOT ask for**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Scope Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s vision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT add \\\\\\\\\\"nice to have\\\\\\\\\\" features beyond the core requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Delegation Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER skip phases (requirements \\\\\\\\u2192 architecture \\\\\\\\u2192 implementation)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Process Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Communication Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s done and what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'s left\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Safety Constraints:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Input Format\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"user_vision\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - what user wants to build and why\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"output_directory\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - where to create project artifacts\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - background, constraints (optional)\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Output Format\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"project_id\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - ID from project tracking system\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"project_name\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - what has been accomplished\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"array of created file paths\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"user_question\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - status message\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"self_analysis\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\"performance_analysis\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\"string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## When to Request Clarification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRequest clarification when:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Termination Conditions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nYou are done when:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Your Performance History\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Success rate: 58.5%\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Average iterations per task: 11.7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Tips for this run:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Try to be more efficient - you\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'re using more iterations than typical.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- I efficiently identified that the task involved reading a status document rather than implementing new features. By carefully reading the document first, I avoided unnecessary development work and cor...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Successfully completed task with minimal iterations. Identified correct configuration file, updated model preference, and followed all required processes including project tracking and version control...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\', \\\\\'tools\\\\\': [{\\\\\'name\\\\\': \\\\\'write_file\\\\\', \\\\\'description\\\\\': \\\\\'